  "baseline_commit": "cbc9a7f",
  "scope": "Stage 5d: adaptive k integration of kappa_xy / T for curvature concentrated near small gaps and zero modes.",
  "decision": "User decision 2026-09-30 (recommendations adopted): kappa_xy / T only (no adaptive Chern integration); optional argument thermal_hall(..., integration=AdaptiveIntegration(...)); provisional defaults relative 1e-3, absolute 1e-7 (k_B^2 / hbar), 2e5 points, depth 12.",
  "method": "Cells in reciprocal-basis fractions start as the result mesh. Each cell holds its midpoint value and the midpoint values of its four quarters; |quarters - midpoint| is its error estimate and the Richardson combination (4 quarters - midpoint) / 3 its value. The cells holding half of the total error are split (Doerfler marking; 20 new points per split) until the total error estimate is below max(absolute, relative * |kappa / T|) at every temperature, the budget is spent, or only cells at the depth limit remain. H(k), dH/dk and the Colpa diagonalization are evaluated at new momenta; the integrand is the shared pair-form kernel of 5c.",
  "added": {
    "code-space/spintoolkit/observables/berry.py": "AdaptiveIntegration, thermal_hall(integration=...), ThermalHall.integration diagnostics (error estimate per temperature, points, convergence, stop reason, cells at the depth limit, largest-error cells, smallest particle gap)",
    "code-space/spintoolkit/definitions/defaults.py": "TOPOLOGY_ADAPTIVE_RELATIVE, TOPOLOGY_ADAPTIVE_ABSOLUTE, TOPOLOGY_ADAPTIVE_MAX_POINTS, TOPOLOGY_ADAPTIVE_MAX_DEPTH",
    "code-space/tests/test_methods/test_berry.py": "3 adaptive tests (23 in the file)",
    "examples/lswt_stage5d_check.py": "this record"
  },
  "findings": [
    "Narrow gaps (Haldane D = 0.01, 0.003, 0.001, t = 0.3): the adaptive result differs from the uniform 2048 x 2048 two-band reference (4.2e6 points) by 1.8e-8, 8.8e-10, 9.5e-10 with 57k, 77k, 92k points; the uniform 12 x 12 mesh is 23-49 percent off and 1024 x 1024 still 1.6e-4 (relative) off at D = 0.001.",
    "The error estimate bounds the actual error in every reference case and is conservative by 10^2 to 10^4 (it is the unextrapolated difference while the value is extrapolated).",
    "Smooth integrand (D = 0.2): the uniform midpoint rule on the periodic zone is exponentially accurate (12 x 12 exact to 1e-10); the adaptive cubature is second order locally and spends 24k points there. Adaptive integration is for sharp features, not a general replacement.",
    "Kitaev [111] h = 2: adaptive equals uniform 192 x 192 within 4e-7 (relative) with 43k points.",
    "NBCP (J_PD or J_Gamma = 0.01 meV): with the default budget (2e5 points, about 100 s per state) the error estimates are 0.1-0.35 percent and three of four cases stop at the budget; a 1e6-point run (about 500 s) converges and reproduces the 2e5-point values to six digits (Y J_PD identical, V J_PD within 1e-6), so the actual error is far below the estimate. The uniform 192 x 192 values of stage 5b were off by 1-4 percent (J_PD), and Y J_Gamma by 27 percent at N = 192.",
    "Accidental zero modes at Gamma (linear dispersion E ~ 0.16 |q| meV for Y J_PD): the integrand grows as 1/|q| (4.1, 41, 413 at |q| = 1e-2, 1e-3, 1e-4 in fractions), an integrable singularity in two dimensions, so kappa is finite within LSWT; the refinement reaches the depth limit there with a small remaining error. A physical pseudo-Goldstone gap (beyond LSWT) would cut it off.",
    "Coplanar triangular 120 degrees: kappa stays zero (3e-18) with 720 points."
  ],
